   "line": [
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "We've got very nice central control. White's e4 break isn't a threat — we outnumber it three defenders to two attackers.",
   "teaches": [
    "count the central break"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 266.5,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pbpn1ppp/1p1b1n2/3p4/3P4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 2 10",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The queen's knight goes to d7, never c6 — c6 would block our own c-pawn and hem the bishop in further. And a6 is often useful to take the sting out of a knight jump to b5.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "knight to d7, not c6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 287,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pbpn1ppp/1p1b1n2/3p4/3P4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/R1BQR1K1 b - - 3 10",
   "line": [
